## Why This Question Is Asked
This problem evaluates a candidate's ability to construct precise 3-valued assignments with exact unknown counts under Kleene semantics, along with a practical backtracking strategy for constraint satisfaction.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene 3-valued logic semantics
- Exact unknown count in constraint satisfaction
- Propagation and backtracking in three-valued logic

## Code Example
```javascript
function not(v) {
  return v === 'T' ? 'F' : v === 'F' ? 'T' : 'U';
}

function imp(a, b) {
  return not(a) === 'T' ? b : not(a);
}

function evaluate(expr, vars) {
  if (Array.isArray(expr)) {
    const [op, left, right] = expr;
    const l = evaluate(left, vars);
    const r = evaluate(right, vars);
    if (op === 'and') return min(l, r);
    if (op === 'or') return max(l, r);
    if (op === 'imp') return imp(l, r);
  }
  return vars[expr];
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests temporal extension of 3-valued reasoning with forward/backward propagation and fixed-point thinking.

## Key Concepts
- Temporal 3-valued logic with Kleene semantics
- Implication as ¬A ∨ B across time slices
- Forward-chaining propagated to fixed point

## Code Example
```javascript
function propagate(states, rules){
  let changed=true;
  while(changed){
    changed=false;
    for(const r of rules){
      const a = evalExpr(r.ante, states);
      const b = evalExpr(r.cons, states);
      const out = imp(a,b); // Kleene A→B
      if(states[r.target] !== out){ states[r.target] = out; changed=true; }
    }
  }
  return states;
}
```

